Z||000003||KillerX||11-19-2001||05:41 PM||||hey im doing (trying to do) a competition car with my fiero...im also trying not to cut any holes in the firewall...im trying 2 12" Phoenix gold Xmax subs in the back of each seat. the reason why i went with XMAX is because its a wicked sub and it can sound good even with .5 cubic feet. its not a cheap sub (its like 650 CDN ) but im sure theres other subs thatll do da job. ill let ya know how it turns out im uplading my page tonight so ill have pics...<BR> <A HREF="http://Www.Sweetride.8k.Com" TARGET=_blank>Www.Sweetride.8k.Com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||11-19-2001||06:40 PM||||Thanks for the info.<P>I may end up having to construct my own enclosure.  I'll have to climb around in the car to decide where to put it.<P>I doubt it will really take a big sub considering how small the Fiero's compartment is.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||07:34 PM||||How do you feel about removing the spare tire and jack?  If you don't mind, a single 12" will sound great in that location with a port or 2 going into the cabin.  If you want to put in an 8" it will fit up in the passenger footwell next to the housing for the heater core.  The other option is to go with 1/2 8"/10"/12" subs that need small enclosure space, and put a box behind the passenger seat, or both seats.  Right now I'm in the process of making a box to go behind the passenger seat for my Pioneer IMPP 10".  I had it in there with the box at first, but it was huge.  I'm cutting it down, and will fit much nicer, with the seat hardly moved forward at all.  Those are the best options for a sub that doesn't take up a ton of room, and not cutting into the firewall.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||11-19-2001||09:05 PM||||At the risk of redundancy, (I'm sure my pic is in at least 5 of those threads the search turned up) here is the solution I am using. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/pffinterior.jpg"> <BR>It is a Polk Audio 10" in a home made fiberglass and MDF enclosure. Very easy to make (a bit messy) and rocks. Also takes up a minimum of passenger space. I'm 6'6" and have no problem sitting on the passenger side. It takes up no more room then the pedals.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Freshj||11-19-2001||09:20 PM||||Hey stimpy, I don't suppose you have the Dimensions..........||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pyric||11-19-2001||09:21 PM||||Doesn't putting a box behind the seat make it vibrate a lot?  Knew someone who did that in their truck, and after riding with them for 5 minutes, I lost all feeling in my rear end.||||reg||3
Z||000009||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||09:27 PM||||doesn't riding in a Fiero make the seat vibrate a lot?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  lol, I'm just kidding.  The one behind mine isn't noticable at regular volumes, and I've had nothing but compliments on a great massage from people sitting there with it turned up loud.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
